Bundled receiver plugin
-----------------------

From milestone M4 on, a release of this integration ships the Enigma2 receiver plugin as an
IPK package inside the release artifact, so that the integration can install it on a box over
SSH.

That plugin is a SEPARATE PROGRAM. It is licensed under the GNU General Public License,
version 2 or (at your option) any later version, because it imports and runs inside enigma2.
Bundling it here is mere aggregation: it is not linked into, derived from, or combined with
the Python code of this integration, and the MIT license of this repository does not apply
to it.

  Plugin:   enigma2-plugin-extensions-mqttbridge
  License:  GPL-2.0-or-later
  Source:   https://github.com/deltasystems-pl/enigma2-mqtt-bridge

Every integration artifact that contains the IPK also contains its complete corresponding source
archive, including the GPL license. `bundled/metadata.json` records the exact source commit and
the SHA-256 and size of both archives. Development builds may deliberately bundle a reviewed,
pinned commit newer than the last plugin tag while both still report `0.1.0`; they do not claim
that commit is the tagged release. Published integration releases pin an immutable public plugin
commit, and their CI rebuilds and byte-compares the IPK and source archive before publishing.

